WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.940
A recent study revealed that about 2 million kids

2
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:07.980
are going to sleep each night without a bed of their own.

3
00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.890
Well, after our next guest learned about this need

4
00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:15.040
he decided to start building beds for kids in his community.

5
00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:16.760
And six years later,

6
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:21.760
he has provided over 400 beds to families,

7
00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:25.120
and his name is Robert Bosquez,

8
00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.920
and he's an elementary school custodian,

9
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:32.350
and I am so honored that he is joining us today.

10
00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:33.620
Robert.

11
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:36.300
(audience cheering)
Hi Drew, how are you?

12
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.860
Hi Robert.

13
00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:41.250
We're so excited to have you and your community

14
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.670
spotlighted here on the show.

15
00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:45.520
When we read that you said

16
00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.270
there is an invisible need for this,

17
00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:50.440
can you explain that?

18
00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:51.640
How did you learn about this?

19
00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.730
Tell us everything.

20
00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:56.030
Sure, so six years ago

21
00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:57.913 line:15%
when we started this program,

22
00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.590 line:15%
we, myself included,

23
00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:03.480 line:15%
didn't know that there was this hidden need.

24
00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:06.820
So we reached out to a local not-for-profit here in town,

25
00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:08.740
they provide furniture for families here in town,

26
00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:11.040
and we asked them, "What is your number one request?"

27
00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.010
Right away they said beds.

28
00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:14.310
So I was like, "Okay, well, you know what?

29
00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:16.100
Let's do some fundraising.

30
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.830
We fundraise to build 40 beds."

31
00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:21.350
And I said, "Let's put an application out

32
00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:23.240
and let's see how many we get."

33
00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:25.690
And we received over 100.

34
00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:27.030
That told me right there that,

35
00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:29.260
you know what, this need here in town

36
00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:31.770
is a need that we need to fulfill.

37
00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:36.200
And in 2015 you began building and donating beds

38
00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.360
to those families and others.

39
00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:40.940
Like, how does the program work?

40
00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:44.090
So every fall we put an application out,

41
00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:45.250
and once we receive 'em,

42
00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:48.800
we always receive way more than we can provide.

43
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.580
And some of these stories that we hear,

44
00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:53.430
you know, they're so heart touching.

45
00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:55.457
It's difficult to tell a family,

46
00:01:55.457 --> 00:01:58.167 line:15%
"I'm sorry, but we can't provide you a bed."

47
00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:02.160 line:15%
But the rewarding part is when we invite these families.

48
00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.210 line:15%
So we invite these families that are chosen

49
00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:05.713
to come and help build along.

50
00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.210
And the excitement of the families receiving...

51
00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:11.120
you know, some of these kids

52
00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:13.510
are sleeping in a bed for the first time.

53
00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:16.480
And when you make these beds

54
00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.400
I understand that you take care

55
00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.170
of every aspect of it, right?

56
00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:23.540
So they're not just getting a mattress, right?

57
00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:24.373
Correct, yeah.

58
00:02:24.373 --> 00:02:25.980
So when we build we invite 'em to build.

59
00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.800
We build the frame, they get a mattress,

60
00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.730
they get the sheets, they get the pillow,

61
00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:33.800
they get, that was a quilt.

62
00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:37.500
Well, they get laundry detergent, books and a teddy bear.

63
00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:38.840
So they get a whole package.

64
00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.626
It's not just the bed.

65
00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:43.330
Oh, (sighs) I love what you are doing

66
00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:47.510
and thinking of every brilliant touch.

67
00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:52.510
And what is it that you guys are often in need of most

68
00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:54.063
in order to do this?

69
00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.710
Well, as we all know

70
00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:59.450
mattresses are the most expensive part of this.

71
00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:01.770
And recently, you know, last couple of years,

72
00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:04.670
we reached out to a local furniture store here in town,

73
00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:07.070
and this year it's just gonna be hard.

74
00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:10.560
It's gonna be tough because we all know with the pandemic

75
00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.450
everybody has been hit so hard

76
00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:15.280
that the ask this year is gonna be really tough

77
00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:16.780
if we even ask.

78
00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:17.902
I understand.

79
00:03:17.902 --> 00:03:22.902
And our friends at Simmons actually reached out to us

80
00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:25.170
and today they're gonna gift you

81
00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:30.170
30 brand new twin mattresses worth over $7,000,

82
00:03:30.408 --> 00:03:32.210
(audience cheering)

83
00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:36.370
and more friends of ours, Tuft &amp; Needle,

84
00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:41.070
is going to provide 30 sheet sets that are brand new.

85
00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:44.710
I'm so happy, and I thank Simmons and Tuft &amp; Needle

86
00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:46.970
for stepping up to the plate,

87
00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:48.820
for wanting to be a part of this,

88
00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:53.820
for enabling Robert to do what it is that you do.

89
00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:57.320
And you really are a superhero

90
00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:00.820
saving the world one bed, one family,

91
00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:03.130
one whole setup at a time,

92
00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:07.103
and we just thank you so much for that.

93
00:04:07.103 --> 00:04:09.220
(audience cheering)

94
00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:11.270
Thank you Drew for having us.

95
00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:15.310
And I can't thank you enough,

96
00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:17.090
our committee thanks you as well.

97
00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:22.090
Do you ever get to do anything for yourself and your wife?

98
00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:24.870
And I think you guys have an anniversary coming up,

99
00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:26.472
any plans?

100
00:04:26.472 --> 00:04:28.470
No, not yet.

101
00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:31.050
Yeah, well, it's our 25th year anniversary.

102
00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:33.250
My wife is a wonderful human being.

103
00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:34.083
Of course, you know,

104
00:04:34.083 --> 00:04:37.760
none of this is possible without her support.

105
00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:40.640
So as of right now we don't have any plans,

106
00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:44.360
but you know, we'll just sit back and relax

107
00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:46.180
and enjoy our 25th year anniversary

108
00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:47.970
and we'll see what happens next year.

109
00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:50.640
Well, guess what Robert, you have some plans now

110
00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.090
because the IHG Hotels &amp; Resorts,

111
00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:55.120
one of the largest hotel groups,

112
00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:57.920
want to give you and your wife a luxurious vacation

113
00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:02.010
to the InterContinental Presidente Cozumel Resort &amp; Spa.

114
00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:05.680
And it's located right on the coast of Mexico

115
00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:09.280
amid one of the world's largest coral reef systems.

116
00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:11.300
And it's all taken care of

117
00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:13.540
during your six nights seven day trip,

118
00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:16.560
and meals and flights all done,

119
00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:18.580
all you have to do is snorkel and enjoy

120
00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:20.670
and recharge the batteries

121
00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:24.356
so that you can keep doing what you're doing.

122
00:05:24.356 --> 00:05:25.361
(audience cheering)

123
00:05:25.361 --> 00:05:28.320
Oh, (indistinct) thank you so much.

124
00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:29.419
Oh, you're gonna make me cry,

125
00:05:29.419 --> 00:05:33.260
I don't wanna cry.
(Drew laughing)

126
00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:36.590
We're all so inspired by what you're doing here,

127
00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:38.883
and you're so amazing.

128
00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:40.640
Well, thank you Drew.

129
00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:44.410
And again, every year what recharges my batteries,

130
00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:46.300
if I can share this story,

131
00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:48.200 line:15%
we had a family come.

132
00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.260 line:15%
They rented a U-Haul because they wanted to make sure

133
00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:52.380 line:15%
that they had a transportation to take these beds home.

134
00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:54.583
It was two young girls,

135
00:05:54.583 --> 00:05:57.140
and the excitement of these girls

136
00:05:57.140 --> 00:06:00.270
putting these beds together, you could just see it.

137
00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:03.830
And once the bed was finished, we put the mattress on there

138
00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:06.540
and we put all the sheeting and the pillows,

139
00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:08.680
and she took that teddy bear,

140
00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:12.730
she gave it a big bear hug and just fell back into the bed.

141
00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:17.187
And that right there, from that moment on, told me,

142
00:06:17.187 --> 00:06:18.020
"Guess what?

143
00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:19.790
You're gonna be doing this every year."

144
00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:22.873
(audience cheering)

145
00:06:25.372 --> 00:06:28.360 line:15%
Thank you Robert for being you.

146
00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:30.000 line:15%
It's the only thing I can think of.

147
00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.040 line:15%
And if there's any way that you can multiply yourself

148
00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:35.890 line:15%
or teach us all how to be more like you,

149
00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:37.350
please do so

150
00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:39.180
'cause you're amazing.

151
00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:41.510
Well, go to our website to learn more

152
00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:43.770 line:15%
about Robert's Bed Blitz program

153
00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:45.360 line:15%
so that you can get involved.

154
00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:46.720 line:15%
We want to,

155
00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:49.900
Simmons and Tuft &amp; Needle are getting involved,

156
00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:52.770
and it's it's game on

157
00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:55.677
all in honor of Robert and his incredible work.

158
00:06:55.677 --> 00:06:58.260
(lively music)

